        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. French ministers discuss measures to better deal with child abuse cases France Issued on: 09/06/2026 - 15:04 Modified: 09/06/2026 - 15:05 Amid public outrage growing over the kidnapping and murder of 11-year-old Lyhanna, French ministers have held an emergency meeting to discuss measures aimed at better dealing with sexual offenders and child abuse cases. FRANCE 24's James André is at prime minister's residence, and tells us more. French State and Justice Minister to be sued for 'gross negligence' over girl's rape 09/06/2026 France French State in turmoil as it faces criticism over child protection 09/06/2026 France France's justice minister decision not to resign 'may well be taken out of his hands' 08/06/2026 France French justice system 'overwhelmed': 'Systemic' failures tackling violence against women & children 08/06/2026 France French government 'under pressure' amid public outcry over children protection failures 08/06/2026 France Town marches in honour of girl whose killing sparked public outcry 08/06/2026 France Missing girl case exposes flaws in judicial system, expert says 07/06/2026 France A look back at French former first lady Bernadette Chirac's legacy 06/06/2026 France Bernadette Chirac, former first lady of France, dies aged 93 06/06/2026 France"
